31
00:15:16,087 --> 00:15:22,727
And these futures could be the member methods and also the data member fields.

32
00:15:23,307 --> 00:15:23,447
Okay.

33
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:34,660
And so the inheritance relationship is one of the important object relations in object-oriented programming.

34
00:15:35,259 --> 00:15:40,720
And you can do the inheritance relationship in different ways.

35
00:15:41,180 --> 00:15:47,600
You can do it by using the regular classes, you can use abstract classes, or you can use interfaces.

36
00:15:48,244 --> 00:15:52,584
Now, I'm going to start with the regular classes and then continue forward.

37
00:15:53,744 --> 00:16:05,584
Okay, now this is the UML representation of the inheritance relationship.

38
00:16:06,584 --> 00:16:09,043
As you see here,

39
00:16:09,940 --> 00:16:30,680
There is a class A and there is a class B and class B extends from class A. A is the parent class and B is the child class. And the direction of the arrow is pointing to the parent class. So this basically means that

40
00:16:31,124 --> 00:16:38,223
instances of class B inherits from the instances of class A.

41
00:16:38,223 --> 00:16:47,443
So basically, so when you read this, you will read it like B inherits from A.

42
00:16:47,744 --> 00:16:52,744
So therefore, the arrow points to the parent class.

43
00:16:53,364 --> 00:16:53,504
Okay.

44
00:16:53,824 --> 00:16:57,483
Sometimes we call this parent class a super class or base class.

45
00:16:57,723 --> 00:16:59,124
And sometimes we call the...

46
00:16:59,124 --> 00:17:05,564
A child class, a subclass, or drive class in different tutorials or in different sources.

47
00:17:07,859 --> 00:17:21,119
And when you create a relationship like this, all member fields, data member fields, and the methods of the parent class are transferred to the child class.

48
00:17:21,119 --> 00:17:30,659
Okay. However, children cannot access the inherited private members. So what does this mean?

49
00:17:34,228 --> 00:17:38,768
The child class can, will have its own methods.

50
00:17:39,388 --> 00:17:44,048
In addition, the child class can use the parents' methods as well.

51
00:17:44,268 --> 00:17:47,688
So, because it will inherit all the methods that the parent has.

52
00:17:48,588 --> 00:17:53,008
Also, the child class will have its own data member fields.

53
00:17:53,128 --> 00:17:58,628
In addition, it will have data member fields of the parent class as well.

54
00:17:58,628 --> 00:17:59,428
Okay.

55
00:17:59,988 --> 00:18:23,648
But if the parent class data member fields are defined as private, in that case, even the child class will have to use parent class public member methods in order to access the data in the privately defined member fields.

56
00:18:23,648 --> 00:18:24,367
Okay.

57
00:18:27,827 --> 00:18:40,347
If you want data member fields to be accessed by the child class, in that case, there is another access modifier, which you haven't learned.

58
00:18:40,468 --> 00:18:44,407
We discussed it, but we haven't gone into details.

59
00:18:45,268 --> 00:18:47,688
There is a protected access modifier.

60
00:18:48,211 --> 00:18:54,451
Just like the public or private, there is another access modifier protected.

61
00:18:54,451 --> 00:19:08,052
And this basically allows the child classes to access the parents' data member fields if they are defined as protected.

62
00:19:13,107 --> 00:19:33,967
Okay. Now, so what are the rules when we create inheritance relationship? So as you see here, there is an inheritance relationship, there is this person, and from this person, three classes are extended, student is extending the person, employee, and retired.

63
00:19:35,412 --> 00:19:44,052
And then director and the part-time employees are extending the employee class.

64
00:19:45,451 --> 00:19:45,572
Okay.

65
00:19:46,672 --> 00:19:49,531
Now, so what are the rules?

66
00:19:50,052 --> 00:20:00,000
Subclasses cannot reject a member from the superclass, which means that if there are some methods here and data member fields here, student class...

67
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:10,400
will inherit it by default. So in student class, we cannot say, like, I will not use such and such method in person class.

68
00:20:10,400 --> 00:20:17,360
Okay. So the subclasses cannot reject members from the superclass.

69
00:20:20,468 --> 00:20:26,788
However, the methods in the superclass can be changed in the child class.

70
00:20:27,288 --> 00:20:31,708
So, for example, let's say if there is an introduced self method in the person class.

71
00:20:32,096 --> 00:20:40,396
I can have an introduce self method in the student class, which will then overwrite the introduce self of the person class.

72
00:20:40,396 --> 00:20:51,195
So in that case, when I call an object which is created from the student class, if I call that object's introduce self method,

73
00:20:51,632 --> 00:21:02,612
If both child class and the parent class has the introduce self method, I will be calling the introduce self method of the child class because it will override it.

74
00:21:03,492 --> 00:21:03,692
Okay.

75
00:21:04,211 --> 00:21:06,451
Now, this is called overriding.

76
00:21:07,352 --> 00:21:11,512
Remember, there is another term which is called overloading.

77
00:21:12,012 --> 00:21:16,692
Overloading, so we use the overloading term when we have

78
00:21:16,991 --> 00:21:33,152
Two same name methods in the same class, but their signatures are different. In that case, we call that situation overloading. But now we are using another term, we are calling overriding.

79
00:21:33,652 --> 00:21:46,092
If there is a method in the parent class, and if I want the same name, same signature method in the child class, that method will be override the parents method.

80
00:21:48,231 --> 00:21:51,092
Now, if you want...

81
00:21:51,347 --> 00:22:05,427
A method, if you don't want a method to be overridden in one of the child classes, in that case, in the upper class, in the super class, you can define that method as a final method.

82
00:22:05,427 --> 00:22:16,688
If a method is defined as final method, in that case, that method cannot be overridden in the subclasses.

83
00:22:19,827 --> 00:22:36,487
Okay. Now, if you create inheritance relationship, there is a, so if you go high in the tree in the inheritance relationship, basically, you are, you observe generalization.

84
00:22:36,948 --> 00:22:43,768
So, which means that the class in the root of the tree is as general as possible.

85
00:22:43,768 --> 00:22:50,568
If you go to the leaves of the tree, in that case, you are doing specialization.

86
00:22:51,248 --> 00:22:59,628
And in that case, if you go to the leaves of the inheritance tree, so you will find specialized classes.

87
00:22:59,868 --> 00:23:02,108
They will have some methods that are specialized.

88
00:23:02,672 --> 00:23:05,932
For particular purpose.

89
00:23:07,011 --> 00:23:07,251
Okay.

90
00:23:12,596 --> 00:23:20,895
Now, let's take a look at, so this inheritance is also called generalization and specialization relationship.

91
00:23:20,895 --> 00:23:30,556
And the superclasses are generalized classes and the child classes are specialization classes.

92
00:23:31,135 --> 00:23:36,635
And the relationship between the parent and child is a relationship.

93
00:23:39,791 --> 00:23:47,271
So we said that association, aggregation, composition, they are all ownership-based relationship.

94
00:23:47,971 --> 00:23:55,531
So which means that one object of a class owns the object of the second class.

95
00:23:55,791 --> 00:23:55,951
Okay.

96
00:23:56,451 --> 00:23:58,711
So there is this ownership relationship.

97
00:23:58,711 --> 00:24:02,711
But in inheritance relation, there is a relationship, which means that...

98
00:24:03,539 --> 00:24:11,819
The objects of the child class is also a car, object of car class.

99
00:24:11,819 --> 00:24:22,359
So, which means that the type you can use, for example, if you create an object of the station wagon class,

100
00:24:24,660 --> 00:24:28,480
You can use the station wagon as the type of that object.

101
00:24:28,660 --> 00:24:33,980
Also, you can use the car class as the type of that object because there is a relationship.

102
00:24:34,600 --> 00:24:52,180
For instance, if you create an object of the dot matrix class, in that case, you can also use the printer as the type of that object because that object is a dot matrix object and as well as it is a printer object as well.

103
00:24:52,660 --> 00:24:53,960
There is a relationship.

104
00:24:57,940 --> 00:25:03,860
And the child can be used whenever the parent is expected.

105
00:25:04,440 --> 00:25:18,360
So, for example, since I created, in the examples that I just gave you, if I created an object of the station wagon, and in that case, for that object, I can use the parent as the type.

106
00:25:25,940 --> 00:25:28,320
parent as the type. Okay?

