01:50:45,235 --> 01:50:54,735
Okay, so lastly, so to wrap up, so why do we use interfaces instead of abstract classes?

713
01:50:54,735 --> 01:51:04,015
The reason is that Java or any other object-oriented programming language does not support multiple level of inheritance.

714
01:51:04,756 --> 01:51:08,136
So every class extent only one class.

715
01:51:08,656 --> 01:51:18,256
But if you wanted to have an object have a multiple view, in that case, we might want to use interfaces.

716
01:51:18,936 --> 01:51:19,256
Okay.

717
01:51:20,564 --> 01:51:34,184
And the second reason that we are using interfaces is that if there are a lot of methods, then the abstract class is more useful because we can provide a default implementation for some of the methods.

718
01:51:34,543 --> 01:51:42,384
OK, so this is the reason, benefit of using the abstract class as opposed to the interface class.

719
01:51:42,684 --> 01:51:48,463
So if in the super class, if there are so many methods, in that case, you might want to.

720
01:51:48,564 --> 01:51:51,844
implement some of those methods in the superclass.

721
01:51:52,583 --> 01:52:03,384
In that case, using abstract is better because in interfaces, you cannot implement the methods in the superclass.

722
01:52:07,155 --> 01:52:19,876
And if the base class keeps on changing, then the interfaces can cause issues because we cannot declare additional methods to the interfaces without changing the all implementation classes.

723
01:52:20,467 --> 01:52:29,527
But with the abstract class, we can provide default implementation and only change the implementation classes that are actually going to use these need methods.

724
01:52:29,647 --> 01:52:39,907
So which means that if you use interfaces and if you make a change in interfaces, every other class that implements those interfaces needs to be changed.

725
01:52:40,404 --> 01:52:47,464
But if you use abstract classes, in that case, you can add some regular methods to the abstract classes.

726
01:52:47,464 --> 01:52:56,923
In that case, the methods that are extending the abstract class, they only implement the abstract classes.

727
01:52:57,744 --> 01:53:03,084
So therefore, there won't be any change necessary.

